This namelist computes the thermal history of the mean-density gas in a uniform
universe (pancake setup with delta_ini=0), from z=2000 to z=0, without gravity
and without particles.
To compile the code, type in folder /bin the command line:
make NDIM=1 UNITS=COSMO HYDRO=1 NION=3 INIT=PANCAKE
Then execute the code in the parent folder, saving the log file:
bin/ramses1d namelist/thermal_history.nml > thermal_history.log
In a serial 1D run, each output (aout) is printed in the log file instead of
being written to disk, including the ionization fractions with neq_chem.
The temperature history is then extracted from the log file with:
python3 utils/py/thermal_history.py thermal_history.log
The default is non-equilibrium chemistry (neq_chem) with the Haardt and Madau
UV background switched on at z_reion.
For equilibrium cooling, set cooling=.true. and neq_chem=.false. in the
COOLING_PARAMS block. The HM12 tables are read from ./data/HM12:
link utils/data as data in the run directory (ln -s utils/data data).

&RUN_PARAMS
cosmo=.true.
hydro=.true.
nrestart=0
ncontrol=1
da_over_a_max=0.01
verbose=.false.
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
